<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104259" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τομοῦροι</span></b> , οἱ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>priests of Zeus</i> at Dodona,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ μέν κ᾽ αἰνήσωσι Διὸς μεγάλοιο
				Τομοῦροι,</span> an ancient reading for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θέμιστες</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				16.403
			</span></i>, v.
			<i><span class="en">
				Str.
				7.7.11
			</span></i>, who explains it as a shortd. form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τομάρ-ουροι,</span>
			<i>guardians</i>
			<i>of Mount Tomarus,</i> cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τόμαρος;</span>
			 the variant is given as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τόμουραι</span> by <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1760.47
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1806.37
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόμουρε</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάντι</span>
			 occurs in <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				223
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>